    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db2e5f26_346089a4",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-18T21:39:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need to use the highspeed timer while cr50 is awake, but it does not run while cr50 is asleep. So we need the low speed one to update the high speed one and to be able to trigger events during sleep.",
      "parentUuid": "db2e5f26_611f2172",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a4238a3d15850651793a1e139632a334d0c4c14a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db2e5f26_14a22da3",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000229
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-18T21:44:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand what you are doing, I don\u0027t understand why: what is the problem with having just timels used for time counting, running all the time, sleep or no sleep? Why not do that?\n\nYou might have good reasons, I just don\u0027t understand/know them.",
      "parentUuid": "db2e5f26_346089a4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a4238a3d15850651793a1e139632a334d0c4c14a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db2e5f26_f7b1b3a9",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-18T21:55:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess we could right now. I think we would need to use both of the low speed timers. One to keep track of the system time and the other to set rtc_alarms.",
      "parentUuid": "db2e5f26_14a22da3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a4238a3d15850651793a1e139632a334d0c4c14a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b24e748_8be5b8d0",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1126264
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-18T21:56:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so timels just has lower resolution and is not a perfect integer (~4uS).  Depending on whether software cares about that, it can be a little undesirable (I guess since we\u0027re not a radio chip, the accuracy probably doesn\u0027t matter as much).\n\nIn the future, we may slow the clock even more due to power reasons (so you can expect a resolution of \u003e30uS).",
      "parentUuid": "db2e5f26_14a22da3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a4238a3d15850651793a1e139632a334d0c4c14a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
